+++
title: Coaching your Intimate Self
subtitle: Sex Coaching | Intimacy Coaching | Relationship Coaching | Fantasy Exploration
hook: Have you ever said out loud, to anyone, exactly what you want?
hook2: How do you ask a partner to give you what you need, if you don't know yourself?
+++

Our aim is to help you to really get in touch with yourself as a sexual being, alone or partnered. To help you uncover the deep and secret fantasies that you have, to be able to talk about them, and to act on them. To help you step beyond the shame and guilt limitations that have held you back.

We live in a world that tells us how to be sexual, but rarely how to be. We are taught to be polite, efficient, and modest. But intimacy requires something different. It requires vulnerability. It requires the courage to say, “This is what I want,” even if your voice shakes.

Have you ever had a good sexual experience ruined after it was done because your partner just left, or rolled over and went to sleep? Sex, even the most basic, is an act of vulnerability and opening, and that deserves to be treated with respect. Your partner should be helping you come back to your more typical state of being, rather than leaving you exposed in the emotional aftermath.

Shame whispers, “Is this normal?” Guilt says, “I should be doing something else.” We are trapped in a cultural loading that has been imposed into our thinking, our values, and our belief of what is even possible for us to want, let alone to do. We lack words for what we want unless we are lucky enough to trip over them in overheard conversations around us, or in porn and erotica if we are brave enough to explore these things. We are rarely even taught how to have conversations with partners about consent and ‘traditional’ sex, let alone how to step outside the conservative expectations imposed by cultural norms. We often navigate our romantic lives without a manual, guessing at what is expected of us.

The one escape is that what we see, we can believe. Porn, erotica, smut, snippets in popular movies, and joking references in mainstream shows show us possibilities. They don’t teach how to have conversations about these things, and far too often they make fun of them. Many of these things are strongly gender-biased in presentation, showing us a fantasy that rarely matches the messy reality of connection. We offer a safe place to talk about all of these things, bridging the gap between the screen and the sheets.

Questions about your orientation, your interests, your kinks — what do all of these terms really mean? Dark fantasies that you only allow yourself to think about alone in the dark. We are here with unwavering positive regard and respect for you.

Have you ever explored your body, or a partner’s, with no pressure for sexual outcome or orgasm? Have you ever really let yourself go into sensation and getting lost in the moment with no need to achieve an end?

In our coaching, we strip those expectations away. We replace them with curiosity. We help you uncover the deep and secret fantasies that you have, those quiet things you whisper to yourself in the shower or imagine when you’re driving alone. It’s not enough to just have the fantasy. We help you to be able to talk about them, and to act on them. There is a massive difference between holding a secret and sharing a desire. When you can speak it, it loses its power to scare you. When you can act on it, it becomes part of your reality.

We want to work from the inside out. Starting with all of these thoughts, curiosities, and fantasies, learning to really connect with your body, to give you language and confidence using it. All of this starts within you, accepting yourself and really trusting that you are normal, that these desires are normal.

There is legacy in our culture, in the field of psychology, of poor decisions in the classification of things as disorders. In an early DSM (Diagnostic Manual), they included many things that are simply fundamental parts of the human experience. One of the most egregious was arousal by new experiences. Consider that all of us, nearly all mammals, and most complex animals are rewarded with a hit of dopamine for new experiences—this is the root of curiosity and exploration in all areas, yet it was listed as a psychological disorder when in the frame of sexual expression. We used to mistake the spark of life for a symptom of illness.

Within the Yomonsni collective, we shake off all influences like that because they are about restricting free expression of adult consensual behavior. That is our only restriction—we will support you with any adult consensual sexual behavior. Homosexual, bisexual, pansexual, heterosexual; consensual power dynamics, role play. Whether you want to keep your sex in the bedroom or bring it into other places, and aspects of your life. Subspace, domspace, aftercare, Safe Sane Consensual (SSC), Risk Aware Consensual Kink (RACK), consensual non-consent, erotic hypnosis, erotic brainwashing, pleasure dom, service sub—the words and terms can be confusing and overwhelming. Do you need to have deep conversations about what consent really means, and who is capable of giving it in what scenarios? We help you decode the alphabet soup so you can use the language that fits your life.

Whether you are solo or partnered, the goal is always connection—connection to yourself, and connection to others. We want to give you a grounding of understanding in what you want, what you enjoy, and what you deserve. This grounding is the foundation of all good intimacy. When you know what you deserve, you stop accepting less. When you know what you enjoy, you can ask for it. This knowledge empowers you to powerfully have these conversations with your current and future partners. No more guessing. No more hoping they “get it.” You become the architect of your own pleasure.

For those ready to go further, we specialize in fantasy exploration, including the realms of Kink and BDSM. This isn’t just about ropes and whips; it’s about the psychology of power, sensation, and trust. It’s about finding that safe space to explore outside the edges. It’s about discovering that when you let go of control, whether by tying someone up or letting them tie you up, ou actually gain a deeper sense of presence. We help you navigate the steep learning curve of kink with confidence, ensuring that whether you are a beginner or a veteran, you are exploring with safety, consent, and joy.

Where you need a safe space to explore outside the edges, we can help with that through one-on-one intimate retreats, where you talk about these experiences directly with your coach. These retreats are designed for deep work. We take you out of the daily grind and into a container where time slows down. In this setting, we can explore your fantasies more fully. We can practice the conversations. We can feel the shift in your body as it finally lets go of the “mind isn’t in the moment” block.

Whether you are looking to overcome a specific fear, try a new kink, or simply reconnect with your sensuality, the retreat offers a sanctuary. It is a place where you can be messy, where you can be vulnerable, and where you can be utterly, completely yourself.

Your Invitation: You are a sexual being. You have desires that are waiting to be uncovered. You have a voice that is waiting to be heard. Don’t let shame or guilt hold you back any longer. Let’s find those deep, secret fantasies together, and let’s bring them into the light. Lets ensure that you are fully connected to, understanding, and accepting of your sexual identity. 



